{
  "rules": [
    "If sentiment is positive (≥0.2) in recent history, model tends to overestimate prices; reduce forecast slope or cap upward movement.",
    "If sentiment is negative (≤0.0), model often underestimates; adjust downward bias by adding 1-2% to forecast baseline.",
    "After a sharp price spike (≥10% from prior peak), model frequently overshoots; apply a 1-3 day lag correction or cap forecast at 10% above peak.",
    "When true outcome shows strong mean reversion (e.g., 3+ consecutive days falling from peak), model overreacts; reduce forecast slope by 20-50% for 3-5 days.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, if history shows volatility >15% over 18 days, model tends to smooth too much; increase forecast variance or add 1-2% upward bias.",
    "If sentiment history includes 2+ consecutive 0.00 values, model often underperforms; add 0.5-1.5% to forecast to compensate for low sentiment bias."
  ]
}
